* "American 5153" preamp, stage 1 of 3 (a three-channel head's service drawing 0070922000, supplied by the user): the input into V1B, the two gain networks that the relay K2
* selects (ONE: C6 / R24 / R22 / R1; TWO: C13 / R25 / R6), V2A, V2B, V3A and V3B (a cathode follower) and the two tone stacks that V3B feeds (stack ONE straight from
* its cathode, stack TWO behind R38 43k), each with its volume. The relays K2 and K3 are the SW_ resistors (1 ohm closed, 1e12 open): channel GREEN (one) is every
* relay released; BLUE (two) energises K2 and K3. Channel RED (three) is the other input stage (stage2.net) and the relay K1 (stage3.net).
* Everything here is as the drawing; the three channels' controls are driven together by amp.json (one set of knobs for the channel in use).

* Rails: X (341 V at idle) and W behind R95 10k.
V VRAIL x 100 341
R R95 x w 10k
C C36 w 0 22u
C C40 x 0 47u

* The guitar and its pickup / cable networks; the signal goes to V1B through R50 (10k).
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k
R RPU1 gin pkb1 1e12
.xfmr LPU1 L=2.5
  W pkb1 in 1 pu
.end
R RPU2 gin pkb2 1e12
.xfmr LPU2 L=5
  W pkb2 in 1 pu
.end
C CPU gin in 110p
R RPL gin in 1e12
R SWK1 in pkk1 1e12
C CCAB1 pkk1 0 200p
R SWK2 in pkk2 1e12
C CCAB2 pkk2 0 400p
R SWK4 in pkk4 1e12
C CCAB4 pkk4 0 800p
R RIN in 0 1M
R R50 in g1b 10k

* V1B and the two gain networks. ONE: C6 (4.7n) into R24 330k and C11 (220p) + R22 220k, R23 33k and the 250k ONE GAIN pot R1. TWO: C13 (750p), R25 180k and the
* TWO GAIN pot R6 (250k) with R26 150k across it. K2-A picks the pot's wiper (ONE: NC, TWO: NO) behind C23 (.1u).
T V1B g1b p1b k1b 12AX7
R R34 w p1b 100k
R R51 k1b 0 1.5k
C C29 k1b 0 1u
C C6 p1b a1 4.7n
R R24 a1 b3 330k
C C11 a1 c11 220p
R R22 c11 b3 220k
R R23 b3 0 33k
R VR1T b3 w1 1
R VR1B w1 0 1
C C13 p1b c13 750p
R R25 c13 d6 180k
R R26 d6 0 150k
R VR6T d6 w6 1
R VR6B w6 0 1
R SW_K2A_ONE w1 m2 1
R SW_K2A_TWO w6 m2 1e12
C C23 m2 g2a 0.1u
R R52 g2a 0 1M
R R53 g2a 0 1M

* V2A, then C35 / R80 into V2B's grid; K2-B puts R55 68k (released) or R35 330k (energised, before R80) to ground.
T V2A g2a p2a k2a 12AX7
R R83 w p2a 100k
R R36 k2a 0 1.5k
C C18 k2a 0 22u
C C35 p2a n5 10n
R R35 n5 s35 330k
R SW_K2B_NO s35 0 1e12
R R80 n5 g2b 390k
R R55 g2b s55 68k
R SW_K2B_NC s55 0 1
R R58V2 g2b 0 180k
T V2B g2b p2b k2b 12AX7
R R77 w p2b 100k
C C24 w p2b 270p
R R54 k2b 0 1.5k

* V3A (R84 390k / R57 180k on its grid, unbypassed 1.5k cathode) and V3B, the cathode follower (R59 430k, R58 150k, R60 430k with C30 .22u on its grid).
C C25 p2b n8 3.3n
R R84 n8 g3a 390k
R R57 g3a 0 180k
T V3A g3a p3a k3a 12AX7
R R85 x p3a 100k
R R37 k3a 0 1.5k
R R59 p3a g3b 430k
R R58 g3b j3 150k
R R60 j3 0 430k
C C30 j3 0 0.22u
T V3B g3b x k3b 12AX7
R R45 k3b 0 100k

* Stack TWO (R38 43k in front): R17 43k + C10 .01 to ground, slope R18 47k, treble C8 470p into R9 (250k), bass C14 .1u and R7 (250k rheostat), middle C2 .022u and R8 (25k
* rheostat), TWO VOLUME R10 (1M).
R R38 k3b t0 43k
R R17 t0 c10 43k
C C10 c10 0 10n
R R18 t0 sl2 47k
C C8 t0 vt9 470p
R VR9T vt9 w9 1
R VR9B w9 b9 1
C C14 sl2 b9 0.1u
R VR7 b9 m9 125k
C C2 sl2 m9 22n
R VR8 m9 0 12.5k
R VR10T w9 w10 1
R VR10B w10 0 1

* Stack ONE (straight from V3B's cathode): slope R16 100k, treble C7 250p into R4 (250k), bass C12 .1u and R2 (250k rheostat), middle C1 .022u and R3 (25k rheostat),
* ONE VOLUME R5 (1M).
R R16 k3b sl1 100k
C C7 k3b vt4 250p
R VR4T vt4 w4 1
R VR4B w4 b4 1
C C12 sl1 b4 0.1u
R VR2 b4 m4 125k
C C1 sl1 m4 22n
R VR3 m4 0 12.5k
R VR5T w4 w5 1
R VR5B w5 0 1

* K3-A (ONE VOLUME to the bus, or grounded when energised) and K3-B (the bus, or TWO VOLUME when energised) into the output node o12. R40 and R21 10M.
R SW_K3A_ONE w5 m3 1
R SW_K3A_GND m3 0 1e12
R R40 m3 0 10M
R SW_K3B_NC m3 o12 1
R SW_K3B_NO w10 o12 1e12
R R21 o12 0 10M
* The next stage's input (the K1 / effects-loop network, 680k) loads this node.
R R_LOAD12 o12 0 690k
